WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:06.950
So Donald Trump is using Corona virus to push
a very nationalist agenda and to fire up the

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:10.390
most rabid ultra nationalists in his base.

00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:15.081
The latest example we already talked about
at the top of the show, which is Donald Trump

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:19.410
announcing on Twitter that all immigration
to the United States is suspended.

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:23.070
Trump tweeted last night, again, just a quick
reminder, quote, In light of the attack from

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:28.340
the invisible enemy, as well as the great
need to protect the jobs of our great American

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:31.210
citizens, I will be signing an executive order.

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:35.350
To temporarily suspend immigration into the
United States, we don't know what temporary

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:36.350
means.

00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:37.350
We don't know the legal basis.

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:39.450
We don't even know if this is legal.

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:45.760
But what we've known for a long time is that
Donald Trump would be as ultra nationalist,

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:49.040
the president, as he could get away with.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:53.940
Not necessarily because these are the policies
that he believes in or that he actually thinks

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:55.670
are the best policies for the country.

00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:56.670
Maybe he does.

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:58.149
Maybe he doesn't, doesn't really matter.

00:00:58.149 --> 00:01:03.430
But because from the start of his campaign,
Donald Trump has positioned himself as the

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:08.609
nationalist candidate and it has worked to
bamboozle voters into supporting him.

00:01:08.609 --> 00:01:15.009
If you go back to the campaign in 2015 and
into 2016, it was China's killing us.

00:01:15.009 --> 00:01:19.450
I know about how to stop us from getting screwed
on trade deals, even though he didn't.

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:21.270
But it was very, very effective.

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:23.149
We don't win anymore.

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:26.249
No more Mexican rapists are going to be coming
here.

00:01:26.249 --> 00:01:28.909
We're suspending Muslim immigration to the
United States.

00:01:28.909 --> 00:01:31.929
It's all nationalist language.

00:01:31.929 --> 00:01:38.560
And from day one at his inauguration, that
language of America first referencing an ugly

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:42.670
nationalist slogan from the mid 20th century.

00:01:42.670 --> 00:01:45.790
There have been endless examples during the
presidency.

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:51.130
But today I want to focus in on what's been
done during Corona virus to push the nationalist

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:52.130
rhetoric.

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:56.869
And before I do that, just remember hyper
nationalism, ultra nationalism.

00:01:56.869 --> 00:02:01.569
This is a common element for lack of a better
term of fascism.

00:02:01.569 --> 00:02:05.649
And as we followed throughout the Trump presidency,
we have a number of different elements of

00:02:05.649 --> 00:02:07.450
fascism that are noticeable.

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:09.560
Trump is not a dictator.

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:15.620
Fascism is a form of far right authoritarian
ultra nationalism, often headed up by a dictator.

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:20.830
It often includes police states and lots of
things that we don't have in American society

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:21.950
right now.

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:24.750
But that hyper nationalism is part of it.

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:26.750
And Donald Trump is very much excelling there.

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:28.380
So let's look at our list.

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:33.960
Under the guise of Corona virus, we've seen
the entire premise of the response from Trump

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:36.990
be focused around China is bad and we are
good.

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:42.710
So we had early on Trump first saying China's
